commit 33e7132d5bba2b872f751029d4ac4b4b8e047388
Author:     Flavio Brasil <fwbrasil@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Sun Aug 2 17:15:54 2026 -0300
Commit:     Flavio Brasil <fwbrasil@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Aug 2 17:31:17 2026 -0300

    [kyo-pod][kyo-ui][build] fix three main-CI flakes
    
    Problem:
    - kyo-pod ContainerOrchestrationItTest "isHealthy returns false in under 500ms"
      asserted a wall-clock budget on a single isHealthy call. isHealthy runs one
      container exec (create+start+inspect = 3 HTTP round-trips); under CI load one
      exec exceeded 500ms and reddened linux-arm64. The failure message blamed the
      retry schedule, but isHealthy never runs the schedule.
    - kyo-doctest-plugin / kyo-compat-plugin scripted suites fail on Windows: the
      nested sbt the scripted reload boots cannot create its Win32 named-pipe
      boot-server lock (error 1336), failing the batch reload before any test runs
      (sbt/sbt#6777). Windows-only; the same suites pass on Linux/macOS.
    - kyo-ui browser suites exhaust Windows sockets (WSAENOBUFS / error 10055):
      withUI bound a fresh ephemeral HttpServer per leaf, so the shared Chrome
      churned hundreds of short-lived origins and their sockets.
    
    Solution:
    - Assert isHealthy invokes the health check exactly once (invocation count via
      AtomicInt) instead of a wall-clock budget: deterministic, no dependence on
      exec latency, and it still guards the single-shot contract.
    - Skip the plugin scripted suites on Windows via Def.taskDyn; their behavior is
      platform-independent and fully exercised on Linux/macOS.
    - Share one HttpServer across the run (SharedUIServer, mirroring SharedChrome):
      withUI stashes the leaf UI in a ref and navigates the shared Chrome to one
      stable URL whose page/WebSocket routes re-read the ref per request. One
      origin, no per-leaf socket churn; also faster (connection reuse).
    
    Notes:
    - UIServerTest (reactive round-trip + sequential-session isolation) passes
      through the shared server on JVM+Chrome.
    - The healthcheck test compiles but is not yet run against a real container
      backend locally (Docker Desktop daemon down on this machine); the assertion
      is deterministic and will validate in CI.
